  "description": "Watch now | Plus, The Most Bullish Signal Just Spoke",
  "body_html": "<div><hr></div><p>Few quick notes, before we begin:</p><ol><li><p>The winning stock is at the end of the video and the end of this article. If you have questions, feel free to tag me in the <a href=\"https://substack.com/chat/3537822\">Main Chat</a>. If you are reading this after market hours, still tag me, I read everything in the morning, and will tag you back with an answer. </p></li><li><p>Check out my <a href=\"https://substack.com/@stocktok/note/c-299499191?r=4z8lgl&amp;utm_source=notes-share-action&amp;utm_medium=web\">Video about Jamie Dimon being the best INVERSE indicator</a>. He was a key indicator that led me to say “load the truck!” back in late 2022. I am incredibly bullish going forward…despite headlines and the market chop the last few months. </p></li></ol><p>Ok, now your favorite stocks, from worst to first:</p><h3>Last Place - Trend is NOT Friend</h3><p>These stocks were immediately eliminated because price is below the 200 day moving average. It is the very first thing I check. </p><h4>Goodyear Tire <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$GT&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>  </h4><p>Price action below the 200 day moving average. Very close to breaking through, but I’d prefer to see it break through, and give at least 1 confirmation bounce that a new trend is intact. It did this back in January, only to be a fakeout. </p><h4>Lemonade <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$LMND&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> </h4><p>Price was below 200 day moving average, just barely. It is forming higher lows, as it oscillates around the moving average, but just by following simple rules, it cannot be put in a top bracket. </p><h4>Toast <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$TOST&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> </h4><p>Price is rejecting off the 200 day moving average. Bad trend since August 2025. Maybe the bottom is in…but we don’t have many strong signals for that right now. </p><h4>FactSet Research Systems <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$FDS&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> </h4><p>Appears to be testing the 200 day moving average, and was just slightly below when I reviewed. Similar to Goodyear Tire, we need a confirmation bounce at least.   </p><div><hr></div><h3>Weakest Relative Strength </h3><p>We do not weak, or underperforming stocks. And thus, I evaluate Relative Strength (RS). Not Relative Strength Index. RS measures an asset's price performance compared to a broader benchmark (like the S&amp;P 500) or its industry peers. My <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stocktok-summary-fc6?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Screener</a> seeks out the highest relative strength assets, as it often indicates institutional purchases and or strong momentum trends. </p><h4>And to be abundantly clear, any of these can go up. My last place stocks can go up. But I have to decide what is <em><strong>best, of this list, today</strong></em>. A lower RS could transform to a higher RS later, however trend has not been as friendly lately. So don’t get butt hurt if I ranked your stock lower.</h4><p>The 5 weakest performers (even if they are going up) of the remaining 12 stocks, relative to the S&amp;P 500 were:</p><h4><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$CHEF&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>  - RS 64.84</h4><h4><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$NTRS&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> - RS 66.07</h4><h4><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$CRWD&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> - RS 66.34 </h4><h4><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$ROKU&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> - RS 66.59 </h4><h4><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$XYZ&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> - RS 66.83  </h4><div><hr></div><p>I know some of you are excited about Webull, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;BULL&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>. But I am going to throw this at in the middle of the list for a fundamental reason…and also preface with: <strong>I have no predictions for this stock</strong>. Heck, I use Webull myself, and love the platform. Here is why:</p><ol><li><p>This stock has been in a long term down trend.  It started spiking up April 2026. My speculation on the rise (along with stocks like <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;HOOD&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>) was it was <em><strong>pricing in the fact that the pattern day trader (PDT) rule was going away in June.</strong></em> You may also recall I mentioned that we have <a href=\"https://substack.com/@stocktok/note/c-292480210?r=4z8lgl&amp;utm_source=notes-share-action&amp;utm_medium=web\">A Ton of New Day Trading Gurus</a> that have popped up online, particularly since June. This is incredibly profitable for brokerages, as most of these gurus, behind the scenes, are <strong>paying exorbitant amounts of trading fees,</strong> and blowing their account because many new traders cannot resist the temptation of using margin. </p><ol><li><p>But what happens when the market really turns? IE, goes into a bear market? All those people walk away, never to return to day trading (or even investing, sadly). Yes, some will stick around, but not the majority. That will be a financial hit down the line for platforms like WeBull. And frankly, if it gets too bad, you may even have a FTX situation (not saying WeBull is trading people’s money similar to FTX, but you never know).</p><p></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p></li></ol></li></ol><p>Again, I have no predictions for WeBull, I open my mouth when I am confident on something. But I do not envision BULL to be in an uptrend forever, and think we are guessing how far it will run, before it likely collapses again. </p><div><hr></div><p>We are down to the last 6 stocks. Here I evaluate, in this order:</p><ol><li><p>Who is profitable?</p></li><li><p>Whose share holders are making more money? Its all about shareholders making more money…unfortunately. </p></li><li><p>What chart has the highest probability setup that will give us “pocket aces”. </p></li></ol><h4>All 6 of these look pretty good, but one stock met all 3 of these requirements, and stood out. It is a clear winning “hand” 👇</h4>",
